veltos-desktop (1.1.0~dev4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Start, the flyouts, toasts and the taskbar in Windows 11's acrylic where
    KWin can blur: light #F9F9F9 / dark #2C2C2C at 85-86 %, a contrast effect
    per mode (light popups were grey, dark ones pale grey).
  * Start without a surface of its own (a second frame inside the popup), Quick
    Settings' page footers and Start's footer as lines, no highlight on the
    first hidden icon.
  * Lock screen: the hint and "Reset password" after a wrong password; the reset
    opens the sign-in screen's reset panel.
  * Sign-in screen: "Reset password" only after a wrong password; Tab goes
    through the reset fields and buttons.
  * First sign-in: ~/.config/plasmarc is written, so the taskbar follows the
    first light/dark switch.
  * At sign-in, a monitor the kernel sees but the desktop does not list makes
    the connectors be probed again (Settings' display-detect).
  * Window frames without the 1 px line around them (light in dark mode, grey
    in light mode): the edge is the window's own colour.

 -- VeltOS Developers <1ahmetfurkandemir@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000

veltos-desktop (1.1.0~dev3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Start has one size (it could be dragged larger and smaller, and resizing
    it brought the system down).
  * A new screen's desktop gets the main screen's picture (same-wallpaper).
  * Safely Remove Hardware's notification shows a USB flash drive.
  * Quick Settings: Windows 11 tiles (white with a hairline in light mode),
    the footer under a hairline; the light taskbar near-white, not grey.
  * Sign-in and lock screens: 3 wrong passwords wait 30 s, then 1 min,
    then 2 min after every further 3.
  * KWin script veltosscreenwatch: when no taskbar is on any screen a few
    seconds after the screens changed (a monitor unplugged), plasmashell
    is started again.
  * Sign-in screen: the account's password hint after a wrong password;
    "Reset password" for accounts with a password reset USB (veltos-auth's
    password-recovery service): the USB, then a new password and hint.
  * Quick Settings' hotspot: why a one-channel card cannot share, and the
    note when a 5 GHz hotspot runs on 2.4 GHz.

 -- VeltOS Developers <1ahmetfurkandemir@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000

